{% comment %}
  Root-relative asset and link prefix.

  This used to be `site.url | append: site.baseurl`, which stamped the
  production host onto every asset URL. The effect was that a locally served
  page loaded its CSS and JS from the live site, so local changes never showed
  up in preview -- and it produced a doubled slash, because site.url already
  ends in one.

  site.baseurl is "" for a user site served at the domain root, so base_path
  resolves to "" and every URL becomes root-relative: correct locally and in
  production. Absolute URLs are still built from site.url where they are
  genuinely needed, in seo.html and the feed.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign base_path = site.baseurl %}
